    "category": "Vibe Coding 101",
    "hookAudio": "Let me explain GitHub in a way that **actually** makes sense.",
    "hookText": "GitHub explained in 30 seconds",
    "hookVisual": "Point at camera on \"you.\" Open hands gesture like you're about to break it down simply.",
    "caption": "Save this if you're building an app right now. You'll thank yourself later.\n\n#github #vibecoding #appdevelopment #learntocode #techforbeginners",
    "scriptBody": "Let me explain GitHub in a way that **actually** makes sense.\n\nThink of GitHub as **Google Drive** but for your app's code.\n\nEvery time you save your project to GitHub\nit takes a **snapshot**.\n\nIf you break something tomorrow\nyou can go back to today's snapshot.\n\nThat's it.\nThat's literally what it does.\nIt saves **versions** of your work so you never lose progress.\n\nIf you're building an app right now\nand you're **not** connected to GitHub --\nyou're one bad update away from losing **everything**.\n\nI've seen someone lose **ten hours** of work\nbecause they didn't have this set up.\nDon't be that person.",
