    "scriptBody": "Lovable, Replit, or Cursor -- which one should you **actually** use?\n\nShort answer? It depends on where **you** are.\n\n**Lovable.**\nIf you've never built anything before, start here.\nMost beginner-friendly.\nYou describe what you want. It builds it.\nBeautiful UI out the gate.\nDownside? Harder to scale. Credits burn fast.\n\n**Replit.**\nMore control. Full coding environment.\nYou can deploy right from the platform.\nGood middle ground.\n\n**Cursor.**\nThis is when you're ready to **level up**.\nCode editor powered by AI.\nMore power. More flexibility.\nBut steeper learning curve.\n\nHere's the path I recommend.\nStart in **Lovable** to get your MVP.\nSave your work to **GitHub**.\nWhen you're ready to scale, move to **Cursor**.\nThat's the progression.",
