    "scriptBody": "I was spending over a **hundred** dollars a month on Cursor.\nNow I spend **twenty**.\n\nHere's the hack.\n\nCursor charges by **usage**. The more you code, the more you pay.\nAnd that bill adds up **fast**.\n\nBut there's an extension called **Codex**\nfrom OpenAI that you can install right inside Cursor.\n\nOnce you install it,\ninstead of using Cursor's pricing,\nit routes through your **ChatGPT** subscription.\nThat's **twenty** dollars a month. Flat.\n\nYou get about **six hours** of coding\nbefore you hit any rate limiting.\nAnd for most people, that's more than enough.\n\nSame tool. Same workflow.\nYou're just not paying the premium anymore.\n\nI showed this to my community\nand **everyone** made the switch.\n\nGo to extensions in Cursor.\nSearch Codex. Install it.\nThat's it. You just saved yourself **eighty** dollars a month.",
