    "scriptBody": "Zapier, Make, or n8n --\nwhich automation tool should you **actually** use?\n\nThree platforms. Different **strengths**.\n\n**Zapier** is the easiest to use.\nSimple \"if this then that\" workflows.\nBest for **beginners** and quick automations.\nBut it gets **expensive** fast as you scale.\n\n**Make.com** -- formerly Integromat --\nis more **powerful**.\nVisual workflow builder. More complex logic.\nBetter pricing at **scale**.\nThis is what most serious automators use.\n\n**n8n** is the open-source option.\nSelf-hosted. Completely **free**. Most flexible.\nBut you need technical knowledge\nto set it up and **maintain** it.\n\nHere's my recommendation.\n\nBeginners -- start with **Zapier**.\nReady to scale -- move to **Make.com**.\nTechnical and want full control -- **n8n**.",
